  Original model reaching P<0.05: 2 / 5; with quality covariate: 3 / 5
  Change in Z: Parkinson +0.05; Schizophrenia +1.33; Alzheimer -0.25; Depression +1.07; IBD -1.77

  Interpretation: the change in Z reaches or exceeds 0.5 for at least one positive control; quality confounding affects the conclusions.
  The ten EWAS need to be rebuilt under the model with the quality covariate, and the forty cross-disease comparisons and the composition matrix re-run.

